<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nandivarman III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nandivarman III was king of the Pallava dynasty from about 846 to 869. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandyas</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tellaru">Battle of Tellaru</a>, a victory celebrated in the Tamil poem <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nandikkalambakam">Nandikkalambakam</a>, and his reign saw active overseas trade, attested by a Tamil inscription at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takua-pa">Takua Pa</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>. He was a patron of Tamil literature and of Shaiva and Vaishnava devotion.</p></div>
